ticket.steps:
1. In the back office, add one or more specific prices (to any product) without specifying a customer restriction (applicable to all customer)
2. Anywhere in the code (e.g., in the initContent of IndexController or in the displayHeader hook of a module), add one of the following line of code : 
```php
(new Customer())->delete();
(new Customer(null))->delete();
(new Customer(0))->delete();
(new Customer('a string'))->delete(); // argument is casted as integer in the method
```
4. Reload the page corresponding to where you put previous code (e.g., the home page in FO)
5. Go back in BO to the product on which you created the specific prices **=> they have been deleted**

- Run PrestaShop 8.X with PHP 7.4; 
- Dump result of Db-<executeS() query ;
- Run PrestaShop 8.X with PHP 8.1 ;
- Dump result of Db-<executeS() query ;
- Strict compare two result.

ticket.bug:
In the Product.php file an error occurs on the following lines:
        array_unshift($result, null);
        foreach ($result as &$value) {
            $value = $value['id_product'];
        }

This code adds null to the beginning of $result and in the first interaction it gives an error when querying the id_product variable because the first value of $result is null

This causes a php error:
Got error 'PHP message: [PHP Warning #2] Trying to access array offset on value of type null .../Product.php..., line 7245

ticket.steps:
Execute this php snippet:

// Enter your code here, enjoy!
        $result=array(array('id_product'=>10));
        array_unshift($result, null);
        foreach ($result as &$value) {
            $value = $value['id_product'];
	    print($value);
        }

You will get this: 
Warning: Trying to access array offset on value of type null in ...

Solution proposal:
       // Move array_unshift to the end
        foreach ($result as &$value) {
            $value = $value['id_product'];
	    print($value);
        }
       **array_unshift($result, null);**

